```c
gsize bufsz = 0;
const guint8 *buf = g_bytes_get_data(fw, &bufsz);
```
Reason:
The variable `bufsz` is initialized to 0 and is not properly set before being used to determine the size of the buffer. This can lead to reading beyond the allocated memory when calculating the checksum, resulting in a read-overflow.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
gsize bufsz = g_bytes_get_size(fw);
guint16 checksum_verify;
g_autoptr(GBytes) blob_hdr = NULL;
```
Reason:
The patch correctly initializes `bufsz` with the actual size of the `fw` data using `g_bytes_get_size(fw)`, ensuring that the buffer size is accurately set before it is used. This prevents the read-overflow by ensuring that all memory accesses are within the valid range of the allocated buffer.

